{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
  "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem at the heart of this case is construing subsections (d) and (e) of 28 U.S.C. 2254 together in a way that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What was the evidence that the State court -- do you say that the State court refused to consider evidence that was proffered to it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Richard P. Bress",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "State provided 120 days to develop the State habeas petition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why wouldn't he have brought that new evidence to the attention of the State court first?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Richard P. Bress",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There were three categories of new facts or new evidence that came in on Federal habeas."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, your argument is dependent on the proposition that the claim that was advanced in the Federal habeas proceeding is a different claim from a claim that was adjudicated on the merits in the State court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth and Tenth Circuits have adopted the rule that we advocated for years. The Sixth Circuit and the Fourth Circuit have adopted that rule for Brady claims, and we haven't seen the flood that supposedly is going to come through the gates."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: I that what it was saying is there is legitimate -- this is a Strickland question. Strickland has two parts. Part A is were counsel inadequate; and Part B is did it make any difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bress",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you look at (e), (e) says that you can get a hearing even if you weren't diligent in State court, if the facts that you need to develop were not reasonably available in State court and if they would prove by clear and convincing evidence that you are innocent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: You mean you're saying that (d)(2), \"unreasonable determination of the facts,\" means the factual outcome. In other words, if the factual outcome is reasonable it doesn't matter if the procedures are inadequate; is that your claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Burnett",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our argument is that, Court, don't use this case to say that, because if the Court uses this case to say that it will be putting its imprimatur on what the district court did in holding a hearing when we don't think it was appropriate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How do you want us to dispose of the case that doesn't, that doesn't do that? What do you want us to do?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask you, so I understand your position on the underlying question if we don't dismiss. Am I correct that the granting of an evidentiary hearing was based on a showing by the Petitioner that he failed to develop facts which might change the result?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Burnett",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f9f192608c1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it can happen, certainly. I don't think it's restricted just to Brady. I mean, I think that it -- it is -- it is the same analysis, no matter what the claim is, it's the same analysis that the Federal court needs to go through to look -- to see whether it can consider new matter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1223",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "4f9f192608c197e4f81b27b16fadde847aa8b0e9f6d68578213145b434454b8d",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-4f9f192608c1-57",
